From faa86f83b12f7f43cdde21f48faf045f9e385c60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:36:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: stop re-adding the known up staircase

borg_think_stair_scum()'s "do I already know this up staircase" loop
used continue where the matching down-stair loop uses break, so a
match no longer stopped the scan and the staircase under the Borg -
already tracked, for example from being seen on the map earlier - was
appended to track_less again, once per visit, until the array filled
and later staircases could not be tracked at all.  Break on a match,
like the down-stair loop.
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index 53d1c144b..59560f0a0 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -403,8 +403,10 @@ bool borg_think_stair_scum(void)
         /* Check for an existing "up stairs" */
         for (i = 0; i < track_less.num; i++) {
             /* We already knew about this one */
+            /* (break, like the down-stair loop above: continuing past a
+             * match re-adds the known staircase as a duplicate) */
             if ((track_less.x[i] == borg.c.x) && (track_less.y[i] == borg.c.y))
-                continue;
+                break;
         }
 
         /* Track the newly discovered "up stairs" */
-- 
